  Quote of the Week:

  Saint Ignatius Loyola, Spanish soldier and founder of the Jesuit Order, 
1522:
  "To arrive at the truth in all things, we ought always to be ready to 
believe that what seems to us white, is black if the hierarchical Church so 
defines it."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Josh the gentle spoke to Mannanan of the grandness of Josh the 
gentle's empire and convinced Mannanan to pledge his services to Josh the 
gentle.  After talking to Mannanan, Josh the gentle judged him (a Dwarf well 
known for Psychic Magic) to have a Pagan, Brave character.
  The wet spring blossomed into a fragrant early summer.  Mannanan's Oratory 
spell fizzled and Mannanan wound up with his face covered with 
psycho-kinetic slime.  Josh the gentle marched on Hindu Kush (#2905) with 
his command.

  An army coming from the empire of Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight entered 
Hindu Kush, hoping to conquer that province ruled by the provincial Eagle 
chieftain and made up of great Mountains.  Josh the gentle commanded the 
attacking armies.  The defenders were commanded by the provincial Eagle 
chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Hindu Kush (2905):

