  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 436th Light Cavalry in reserve.  Standing at the 
ready with his warriors was Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight.  No generals 
were present to lead the forces of the provincial Dragon chieftain.
  Josh the gentle's men, ill-supplied for the desert campaign, suffered from 
thirst.  The provincial Dragon chieftain's men, ill-supplied for the 
tortuous desert campaign, suffered from thirst.  Josh the gentle had used a 
long flanking march to try to suprise the provincial Dragon chieftain.  But 
the gambit was detected, and its only effect was to demoralize 
Josh the gentle's solders considerably.  On the other hand Josh the gentle 
maneuvered his troops against the provincial Dragon chieftain with excellent 
tactical foresight and obtained a tremendous tactical advantage.
  Using his arcane Spell of Oratory, Josh the gentle started with an 
inspiring speech to his troops, which bolstered their courage.
  Across the entire front, the Veteran 352nd Light Cavalry were egged on by 
a band of the Order of Black Knights, who whipped them into a fanatical 
terror with their threats and curses.  They were arrayed against the 348th 
Dragons.  The horses of the 352nd Light Cavalry were frightened by the howls 
of the terrible Beasts they beheld.  The 435th Light Cavalry outflanked the 
undermanned enemy and attacked with full force.  The horses of the 435th 
Light Cavalry were frightened by the Beasts they beheld.  The 436th 
Light Cavalry flanked the enemy lines and attacked with full strength.
  Josh the gentle switched the 358th Warg Riders to the fore, as a strategem 
for a better match-up.  The 348th Dragons swooped down on the 358th 
Warg Riders and attacked without mercy.  The 358th Warg Riders battled with 
the 348th Dragons and smashed their heads as if they were eggplants.
  Josh the gentle's armies shattered the army opposing them with a final 
determined charge.  The 358th Warg Riders destroyed the 348th Dragons.
  Takla Makan was overrun by the forces of Josh the gentle.  The battle 
affected the quality of our forces:  the 435th Light Cavalry was greatly 
inspired by the victory.  We now designate it a proud Crack unit.
  During early winter, Josh the gentle announced a call for recruits in 
Takla Makan and was able to enlist the 448th Dragons to fight for 
Josh the gentle.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight for this 
year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Urians (#228) grew bored with the scenery in Hindu Kush and left for Tien 
Shan.


  Here is the financial report for Josh the gentle's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 57 gold in revenue.  7 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 448th Dragons trained well and improved in quality.  29 gold 
was expended to maintain our armies.  Josh the gentle was left with 44 gold 
in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Moosu, Squire to Mannanan
To: Josh the gentle

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Windy spring blossomed into a fragrant early summer.  Mannanan's Oratory 
spell fizzled and Mannanan wound up with his face covered with 
psycho-kinetic slime.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer came.  Mannanan rode into 
Transoxiana.  Looking to the northeast, one can see a Plain area, which is 
known as Karaganda (#2903).  It is populated by Elves and Lorens rules 
there.  Their Elven warriors traditionally array themselves in the style of 
Bowmen and Light Cavalry.  To the northwest lies a poor Plain area called 
Magnitogorsk (#2803), populated by Werefolk.  It is ruled by no one.  If 
need be, they can call on an army of Were-Beasts to defend their province.  
Mannanan encountered no monster.
  During fall, Mannanan travelled to Tien Shan.  Northeast of here lies the 
poor province of Semopalitinsk (#3003), ruled by no one.  It is said to be a 
Forest province inhabited by Werefolk.  If need be, they can call on an army 
of Were-Beasts to defend their province.  During his coastal explorations, 
Mannanan was swimming in a lagoon when a Mermaid spotted Mannanan from a 
distance.  He spoke to the Mermaid with respectful words, and combat was 
averted.

  With the advent of the early winter season, Mannanan cruised over to Takla 
Makan.  He found an interesting feature in Takla Makan: a Cave (#171) 
inhabited by the Witch.  Legend says the Large Hoard of Gold is hidden here. 
The Witch is a horribly ugly hag capable of strong and evil magic.  While 
adventuring, Mannanan saw no marauding monsters.

  Thy humble servant,   Moosu, Squire to Mannanan


