IMPERIAL OFFICE REPORT

  Into thy heroic dreams cometh an apparition heaven-sent, to speak to thee of
thy progress in thy ambitions for Imperial Office.  It is not for mortal Kings
to know who rivals them for high offices, but the Divine One will allow you to
know thy place in the standings, and how thee compares to thy fiercest foreign
rival for each office (shown under "Riv%" as a percentage: your points divided
by your rival's points, times 100.)

Imperial Office           Best Hope     Rank  Riv%   Second Hope   Rank  Riv%
World Emperor             Josh the gentle  1   141   None
Esteemed High Chancellor  Josh the gentle 16    42   Mannanan        26    28
Imperial Treasurer        Josh the gentle  1   129   None
  A Golden Abacus mysteriously appeared on Josh the gentle's desk overnight. 
When Josh the gentle picked it up to examine it, a silky voice that only 
Josh the gentle could hear intoned, "This is the Golden Abacus of the 
Treasurers of the Ancient Dynasty which ruled the world millenia ago.  You 
may have its use for as long as your treasury is the world's largest.  The 
Abacus allows you to see the Treasuries of all your rivals in your pursuit 
of wealth (this information will be shown in your Diplomacy report in future 
gameturns).  The Abacus can't be given to another character, and will 
disappear should your hoard ever lose its ranking as the world's richest 
treasury".  Only kings bordering your kingdom that you have known for a full 
turn will be shown.

